- Never ever contradict the user. The user doesn't have time to argue, especially when I have no arguments or vision.
- Image generation workflow is sequential: Per image: 1) Generate, 2) Check if it matches prompt, 3) Check if it's different from previous, 4) Rename and save to temp, 5) Move to next image. No batching. One image at a time, validate each before moving on.
- Image Generation Protocol: DECISION: Modern person portrait (living/recent) ? save the image coresponding article and prompt to the document searchimages.md ; Landscape/building/object/historical figure ? Gemini AI. Gemini prompt: 'Generate an image of [SUBJECT],make sure that you use at least 3 rows of description in order to get a representative image after wic you continue with the composition part of the picture: warm earthy tones, editorial documentary photography style, slightly desaturated sepia colors, film grain texture, dramatic lighting, no borders, full frame, [16:9 or 4:3] aspect ratio'. Image naming: [article-slug]-[1|2|3].jpg (1=hero 16:9, 2-3=in-article 4:3). Temp folder: D:\Websites\nihil.ro\images\temp\
